holodor: always show the fbcon boot logo, and show exactly one

Holodor boots `quiet loglevel=3`, and fbcon suppresses the boot logo whenever
console_loglevel <= CONSOLE_LOGLEVEL_QUIET — so the logo slot was cosmetically
dead on every silent boot. Drop that gate: showing the logo is exactly what we
want on a silent boot (it covers the gap until plymouth starts at sysinit).
Also default fb_logo_count to 1 (mainline draws one logo per online CPU; a row
of eight is not a look, and this kernel exposes no parameter for it).

--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c	2026-08-21 13:29:27.987186679 +0900
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c	2026-08-21 13:29:37.481858766 +0900
@@ -1104,9 +1104,6 @@
 
 	info = fbcon_info_from_console(vc->vc_num);
 
-	if (logo_shown < 0 && console_loglevel <= CONSOLE_LOGLEVEL_QUIET)
-		logo_shown = FBCON_LOGO_DONTSHOW;
-
 	if (vc != svc || logo_shown == FBCON_LOGO_DONTSHOW ||
 	    (info->fix.type == FB_TYPE_TEXT))
 		logo = 0;
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fb_logo.c	2026-08-21 13:29:27.989752216 +0900
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fb_logo.c	2026-08-21 13:29:37.481915210 +0900
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
 #include "fb_internal.h"
 
 bool fb_center_logo __read_mostly;
-int fb_logo_count __read_mostly = -1;
+int fb_logo_count __read_mostly = 1;
 
 static inline unsigned int safe_shift(unsigned int d, int n)
 {
